/// REFUSE: Undefined variable 'NeverDeclared'.
///
/// An unresolved name is a catchable run-time error interpreted and invalid C
/// compiled -- issue #4.  Whichever way that is settled, the program must not
/// build: either the name is refused statically, or the compiler emits
/// something that raises.  What it may not do is hand cc a symbol that does not
/// exist.
///
/// This is the clearest case for the harness.  The interpreter already fails
/// here, with the right sentence, so clauses 1 and 2 pass today and clause 3 is
/// the one that catches it.
///
begin
    WriteLn (Str (NeverDeclared));
end
